  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how fast Marcos needs to go in miles per hour to cross the 5-mile lake in 10 minutes, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert the time from minutes to hours:**\n   Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, we convert 10 minutes to hours by dividing by 60:\n   \\[\n   10 \\text{ minutes} = \\frac{10}{60} \\text{ hours} = \\frac{1}{6} \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Set up the equation:**\n   Let \\( v \\) be the speed in miles per hour. The distance is 5 miles, and the time is \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\) hours. The relationship between distance, speed, and time is given by the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time}\n   \\]\n   Substituting the known values into the formula, we get:\n   \\[\n   5 = v \\times \\frac{1}{6}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solve for \\( v \\):**\n   To find \\( v \\), we need to isolate it on one side of the equation. We do this by multiplying both sides of the equation by 6:\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 6 = v \\times \\frac{1}{6} \\times 6\n   \\]\n   Simplifying the right side, we get:\n   \\[\n   30 = v\n   \\]\n   Therefore, \\( v = 30 \\).\n\n4. **State the final answer:**\n   Marcos needs to go at a speed of \\(\\boxed{30}\\) miles per hour to make it across the lake in 10 minutes.",
